{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Them and Pinchas.</b> For he was equivalent to all of them. And why did he go and not Elazar go? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: he who began a mitzvah finishes it. He turned back My wrath and struck the Midianite woman — he shall complete the mitzvah. But Moses, who was raised in Midian and sat by the well, did not go. That is what people say: the well from which you drank water — do not throw a stone into it." "<b>And the holy vessels.</b> These are the Ark and the Headplate (tzitz). And they said in the Midrash that the kings of Midian used to perform sorceries with Bilaam, and they would fly through the air when they saw this war. Moses said to Israel: if you see them performing sorceries, show them the Headplate (tzitz) and they will fall to the ground. And this is what is written: ״ואת מלכי מדין הרגו על חלליהם״ — and the kings of Midian they slew upon their slain — for they fell from the air onto the corpses of Midian and they slew them. And so in the book of Joshua it is written (Joshua 13:22): ״ואת בלעם בן בעור הקוסם הרגו בני ישראל בחרב על חלליהם״." "<b>And the trumpets of alarm in his hand.</b> When they would journey, they journeyed with trumpets, and likewise when they would assemble and when they would go to war — all was with trumpets."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:15.395853020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}